---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Editorial policy" description="How Southwala calculates timings, writes articles, handles sources and corrects mistakes.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <h2>Calculations</h2><p>Panchangam timings and horoscope inputs come from astronomical positions of the Sun, Moon and planets, using the Lahiri (Chitrapaksha) ayanamsa and true local sunrise and sunset. We compare our results with published almanacs. Timings are for the place shown and shift by a few minutes between cities.</p>
    <h2>Traditions and sources</h2><p>Devotional articles draw on the Ramayana, Mahabharata, Bhagavad Gita, Puranas and regional practice. Where a story is told differently in different traditions, or comes from folk telling rather than the main texts, we say so. We explain in our own words and do not copy translations.</p>
    <h2>Astrology and belief</h2><p>Horoscopes are general guidance for each rashi, worked out from the day's planetary positions. They are for reflection, not a prediction about your life, and not a substitute for medical, legal or financial advice. Fasting and health practices are never required, and anyone with a health condition should ask a doctor.</p>
    <h2>News and records</h2><p>Where we report news or public records, we link our sources, attribute claims to whoever made them and say plainly when something is unconfirmed. Allegations against named people are reported as allegations.</p>
    <h2>Contributors and review</h2><p>Each article carries the name of the contributor who covers that subject. Our contributors write under pen names and their portraits are illustrations. Every article is reviewed by the Southwala Editorial Desk before it is published. See <a href="/team/">our contributors</a>.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Found a mistake? Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We fix errors quickly and show an "Updated" date on the article.</p>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No party, politician or brand pays for coverage. Sponsored or affiliate content, when it exists, is clearly labelled.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
